WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.960
[Nathan]
Hey, John.

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.220
[Low self-esteem Nathan]
BOOOO.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.440
[Nathan]
Hey John. So, the other day I was just walking down the

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.620
[Low self-esteem Nathan]
This intro is traaaash.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.400
[Nathan]
This guy's always in here, just telling me I'm not good enough.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.020
[Low self-esteem Nathan]
You look like- you look like Drake's ugly cousin, Derek.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:18.780
[Nathan]
Can't argue with that.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:24.180
[Nathan]
I'm not good at a lot of things.  Most things, some would say. Here's a list of all the things I'm good at, versus

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.520
all the things I'm bad at.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.580
I'm not good at sports, I don't know how to... make pottery. I can't juggle. I'd make a terrible doctor.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.980
[Concerned Patient Nathan]
Just give it to me straight, doc. How is she?

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.920
[Doctor Nathan]
Well, if we're being honest, I don't think she's gonna make it.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:38.700
[Concerned Patient Nathan]
No!

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.580
[Doctor Nathan]
If we're being really honest, your shoes are wack and you smell really bad.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:44.840
[Concerned Patient Nathan]
What?

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.480
[Doctor Nathan]
Like, I could smell you when I walked into this room.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.520
Like, maybe it's best if she died. So she won't ever have to smell you again.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:52.420
[Concerned Patient Nathan]
What?

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.420
[Doctor Nathan]
Now, we're going to have to run a couple more tests to be sure, and it

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.400
-oh, never mind, she's dead.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:00.580
[Nathan]
I can't do a good Kanye impression, but I can do a good impression of Obama doing a bad Kanye impression.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:04.100
[Obama Kanye Nathan]
Now, Yeezy Yeezy Yeezy... uh, just jumped over jumpman.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.040
[Obama Kanye Nathan]
Uh, Kim. Where you at, honey?

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.320
[Obama Kanye Nathan]
No, Michelle, jus- there's no Kim, it was just the video.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:11.400
[Nathan]
But even with the things I think I AM good at, I always feel like I'm not good enough.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.620
Like, there's always that tiny little voice in my head that's like:

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.120
[Tiny voice in Nathan's head Nathan]
You call that a good grade?

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.520
You call that being a good friend?

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.680
You call that a crème brûlée?

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.960
[Low self-esteem Nathan]
You call that a flashback?

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.960
[Nathan]
If you think I'm bad at this, then why don't you just leave?

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.280
[Low self-esteem Nathan]
No, I know you're bad. I just need you to know you're bad.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.300
[Nathan]
My problem is, if I'm not amazing at something, I just tell myself, what's the point of even doing it?

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.960
Like, if I'm not an amazing singer, why sing at all? Why would anyone want to listen to me when they can listen

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.920
to Adele

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.000
to Adele, or

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.420
to Adele, or Shawn Mendes

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.160
to Adele, or Shawn Mendes, um...

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:41.800
to Adele, or Shawn Mendes, um, Crazy Frog?

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:46.660
The thing is, the only way you can be amazing at something is if you practice. But I don't want to be at

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:51.100
that first level, where I'm trash at it. I just hate feeling like the most unqualified person in the room.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:55.340
Which is why I feel so uncomfortable in my... [game show noises] Guess which class it is, guess which class

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.440
it is... All of them. It's all of them.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:04.120
I still vividly remember being a small kid in art class, and another kid, who was just sitting in front of me, out of nowhere just turns arounds and says,

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:09.420
[Another small kid Nathan]
Look at this poor, helpless fool trying to draw his measly giraffe, as I complete my replica of...

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:15.660
Café Terrace at Night by Vincent van Gogh. I wish death upon you and your family, yes, I hope you die.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.760
Hahaha! Class, look at this, let's all laugh, haha! In unison. Hahaha!

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.880
[Nathan]
That was all probably in my head. What actually probably happened was he just turned around and said,

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.860
[Another small kid Nathan]
Oh Nathan, that looks pretty good.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.080
[Nathan]
And then, I started thinking,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:27.860
[Small kid Nathan]
That looks

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:28.820
Good?

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:29.860
He's lying.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:30.820
He hates it.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:31.340
He's taunting me.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.160
I- I- I have to kill him before he kills me.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:39.300
[Nathan]
I wish I had an answer for this problem of not feeling good enough, but, uh, I don't. Uh, it's something I go

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:44.400
through everyday, still. What I'm trying to do right now is just do things. Just do things I love,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.700
regardless of how 'good' I am. And just not care. What's that quote?

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.660
[Nathan]
See, your life is like... rolling...

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.360
[Low self-esteem Nathan]
Oh boy, he's gonna try and make it a food metaphor!
[Nathan]
See, your life is like... rolling...

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.620
A burrito. You got all these things you're good at. You got your rice, you got your beans, you got the succulent

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.940
chicken. The lettuce, the sour cream, the guac.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.320
If the money right.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:18.100
Eating them separately, you might not have not have the best chicken in the world, or the greatest sour cream you

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:22.480
ever tasted. You might not be incredible at this, You might not be amazing at that, but roll them all together

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.420
to make you, and you got a pretty good burrito.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:24.920
to make you, and you got a pretty good person.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.120
Uh! Nailed it.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.020
[Low self esteem Nathan]

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:31.400
[Nathan]
Oh, hey, he's gone. I guess I learned to overcome it. That's what you call a character arc, kids.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.560
That's storytelling.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:33.440
That's writing.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:34.480
Get me on a show!

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:39.800
That's my time here. I hope you enjoyed that. For more food-based inspirational metaphors, follow me on my

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:40.680
YouTube.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.680
YouTube or my Twitter.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.460
I just noticed I'm wearing this, but this is very appropriate.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:47.160
Uh, the cowardly dog, the cowardly human.

